een 94 and 47 is 47.\n</answer>.<|User|>What is the quotient when 94 is divided by 47? Please reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nTo find the quotient when 94 is divided by 47, we can use the standard long division algorithm. This involves dividing the digits of the dividend (94) by the divisor (47) step by step. Let's break it down step by step.\n..\n</think>.\n<answer>.\nTo find the quotient when 94 is divided by 47, we use the standard long division algorithm. We start by seeing how many times 47 can fit into 94.\n```.\n  2\n-----\n47|94\n```.\nFirst, we look at the first digit of the dividend, which is 9. Since 47 is larger than 9, we consider the first two digits, 94.\n```.\n  2\n-----\n47|94\n```.\nNow, we determine how many times 47 can fit into 94. We can do this by performing the division 94 \u00f7 47.\n```.\n  2\n-----\n47|94\n  94\n  ---\n   0\n```.\n47 fits into 94 exactly 2 times because 47 \u00d7 2 = 94. Therefore, the quotient is 2.\n```.\n  2\n-----\n47|94\n  94\n  ---\n   0\n```.\nSince 94 divided by 47 gives a remainder of 0, the quotient is 2.\nTherefore, the quotient when 94 is divided by 47 is 2.\n</answer>.<|User|>What is the remainder when 94 is divided by 47? Please reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nTo find the remainder when 94 is divided by 47, we can use the standard division algorithm. This involves performing the division and identifying the remainder. Let's break it down step by step.\n..\n</think>.\n<answer>.\nTo find the remainder when 94 is divided by 47, we use the standard division algorithm. We start by performing the division 94 \u00f7 47.\n```.\n  2 R 0\n-----\n47|94\n```.\nFirst, we determine how many times 47 can fit into 94. We can do this by performing the division 94 \u00f7 47.\n```.\n  2 R 0\n-----\n47|94\n  94\n  ---\n   0\n```.\n47 fits into 94 exactly 2 times because 47 \u00d7 2 = 94. Therefore, the quotient is 2 and the remainder is 0.\n```.\n  2 R 0\n-----\n47|94\n  94\n  ---\n   0\n```.\nSince 94 divided by 47 gives a quotient of 2 and a remainder of 0, the remainder when 94 is divided by 47 is 0.\nTherefore, the remainder when 94 is divided by 47 is 0.\n</answer>.<|User|>What is the product of 94 and 47? Please reason step by step.<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nTo find the product of 94 and 47, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. This involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. Let's break it down step by step.\n..\n</think>.\n<answer>.\nTo find the product of 94 and 47, we use the standard multiplication algorithm. We start by multiplying 94 by 7 (the units digit of 47) and then by 40 (the tens digit of 47, which is 4 times 10). Finally, we add the two results together.\n```.\n  94\n\u00d7 47\n-----\n  658  (94 \u00d7 7)\n+3760 (94 \u00d7 40, shifted one position to the left)\n-----\n 4378\n```.\nFirst, we multiply 94 by 7:\n```.\n  94\n\u00d7  7\n-----\n 658\n```.\nNext, we multiply 94 by 40 (which is 4 times 10):\n```.\n  94\n\u00d740\n-----\n3760\n```.\nNow, we add the two results together:\n```.\n  658\n+3760\n-----\n 4378\n```.\nTherefore, the product of 94 and 47 is 4378.\n</answer>",
